Three things this table says that the twelve printed rows did not:

  * The warming is not one sensor. Every populated tsens zone moved the same way, and C-A is positive
    on 25 of the 38 rows (the other 13 are 0.0). The battery, the eMMC, pa_therm0/1 and the pm8994
    rails barely moved (+0.5, 0.0, 0.0, +0.5), so this is the SoC and not the chassis being warmed from
    outside.
  * Nine zones read 0.0 in ALL THREE windows (xo_therm_buf, DLMt_APC1 and the seven LLM_*). A zone that
    reports 0 in every window is a zone whose delta is exactly 0 and which therefore enters the delta
    table as a real row -- and it is not "cool", it is UNREAD. They cannot change a verdict (0 is not
    the maximum here), but a reader counting rows would.
  * The A column's hottest tsens zone is thermal_zone18 (tsens_tz_sensor17) at 42.7 C, NOT the zone
    with the largest B-A. The instrument's headline is the maximum of B-A, so the three numbers it
    prints (40.9 / 47.7 / 48.0) belong to ONE zone -- thermal_zone12 -- and calling them "the hottest
    zone" is wrong in a way that the full table makes visible.
